@startuml gateway-internals
title The Gateway — one process, one port, every client

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #888888
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

rectangle "JARVIS desktop" as D
rectangle "terminal\n(agentd chat)" as T
rectangle "agent app UI\n(browser page)" as B
rectangle "3rd-party client\n(anything speaking the protocol)" as X

package "Gateway  :8787   (presentation/gateway.py — TRANSPORT only, no business logic)" as GW #EAF3FF {

  rectangle "connection gates (in order)\n--\n1. _origin_allowed — a browser page must be\n    loopback / same-host, else close 4403\n2. _authorized — ?token= or Bearer header,\n    else close 4401\n3. _connection_scope — ?scope=agent:<id>\n    marks the socket as an APP connection" as GATES

  rectangle "protocol.py — the wire format\n--\nreq   {id, method, params}\nres   {id, ok, payload}\nevent {event, payload}\n(3 JSON text frames — NOT JSON-RPC)" as PROTO

  rectangle "_dispatch — THE method table\n--\nscoped conn? → stable tier only +\nparams.agentId FORCED to the scope\n~45 methods, one handler each:\nchat.* · sessions.* · agents.* · projects.*\ntools.* · workspace.* · config.* · mcp.*\ncron.* · marketplace.* · notifications.*" as DISP

  rectangle "run management\n--\nRunHandle {runId, abort event, client_id}\nchat.send → mint handle → asyncio task\nsocket drops → abort THAT client's runs" as RUN

  rectangle "_broadcast → _send_all\n--\nevery AgentEvent → one chat.event frame\n→ EVERY authorized socket (fan-out)\nscoped sockets get only their own\nagent's events (_scoped_event_allowed)" as CAST

  rectangle "HTTP on the SAME port\n(websockets process_request hook)\n--\nGET /file?path&token → bytes (ranges ok)\nGET /apps/<id>/ → app agent's static ui/" as HTTP

  rectangle "background subsystems the gateway owns\n--\nscheduler (cron + heartbeat ticks)\nchannel poller (Telegram, …)\nwebhook server (:8788 — the ONE separate port)\nasync MCP discovery · notifier (push + store)" as BG
}

rectangle "AgentService\n(application layer —\nthe ONLY way inward)" as SVC #F0FFF0
rectangle "~/.agentd/gateway.json\n{host, port, pid, token} · 0600\nrendezvous: how CLI / desktop / app-opener\nFIND the daemon + get the token" as RDV #FFF5EE

D -down-> GATES : ws://…?token
T -down-> GATES : ws://…?token
B -down-> GATES : ws://…?token\n&scope=agent:<id>
X -down-> GATES : ws://…?token
GATES -down-> PROTO : parse_frame
PROTO -down-> DISP : Request
DISP -right-> RUN : chat.send only
DISP -down-> SVC : every handler calls\ninto the service
RUN -down-> SVC : handle_message(on_event)
SVC .up.> CAST : AgentEvents stream back
BG .up.> RUN : cron / heartbeat / channel /\nwebhook runs use the SAME path
GW -right-> RDV : written at bind

note bottom of GW
  The gateway is the daemon's front door — and its ONLY one. Every client
  (desktop, CLI, app UI, a future cloud browser) speaks the same frames to
  the same port. It adapts transport (sockets, HTTP, auth, fan-out) and
  delegates ALL real work inward. Nothing behind it knows what a socket is.
end note
@enduml

@startuml rpc-mechanics
title RPC mechanics — one connection's life, frame by frame

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

participant "Client A\n(the caller)" as C
participant "Gateway\n_handle_conn" as GW
participant "_dispatch\n(method table)" as DISP
participant "handler\n(_sessions_list, …)" as H
participant "AgentService\n+ engine loop" as SVC
participant "Client B\n(another connected client)" as C2

== connect ==
C -> GW : WebSocket CONNECT\nws://127.0.0.1:8787/?token=T (&scope=agent:demo)
GW -> GW : origin gate → token gate → scope tag\nclient_id = uuid4 (tags every run this socket starts)

== handshake ==
C -> GW : req {id:"1", method:"hello",\nparams:{protocol:1, client:"my-app/0.2"}}
GW -> DISP : parse_frame → Request
DISP --> C : res {id:"1", ok:true, payload:{protocol,\ncompatible, agents[…], model, sessions, …}}

== any plain method (sync request/response) ==
C -> GW : req {id:"2", method:"sessions.list", params:{…}}
DISP -> DISP : scoped? → stable-tier check\n+ params.agentId = scope (forced)
DISP -> H : _sessions_list(params)
H --> DISP : payload dict
DISP --> C : res {id:"2", ok:true, payload}
note right of DISP
  A handler exception NEVER kills the socket:
  it becomes res {ok:false, payload:{error:"…"}}.
  ids are client-chosen; the reply echoes yours —
  that's how the SDK matches responses to calls.
end note

== chat.send — the ONE async method ==
C -> GW : req {id:"3", method:"chat.send",\nparams:{sessionKey, message, attachments?}}
GW -> GW : save attachments → uploads/\nmint RunHandle(runId, abort, client_id)
GW --> C : res {id:"3", ok:true, {runId}}  — returns IMMEDIATELY
GW -> SVC : asyncio.create_task(_run)\n→ handle_message(…, on_event=_broadcast)
loop while the run streams
  SVC --> GW : AgentEvent (text delta | tool start |\ntool end + artifacts | …)
  GW --> C : event {"chat.event", {sessionKey, runId,\nagentId, ts, event}}
  GW --> C2 : SAME frame (fan-out to all;\nscoped sockets filtered by agentId)
end
SVC --> GW : agent_end {stopReason}
GW --> C : chat.event: agent_end
note right of GW
  Events are fire-and-forget: no sequence numbers,
  no replay. A client that connects mid-run rebuilds
  from sessions.history. chat.abort {sessionKey}
  cancels via the RunHandle's abort event.
end note

== disconnect ==
C -> GW : socket closes (tab closed, crash, network)
GW -> GW : discard socket + scope\n_abort_client_runs(client_id) —\nruns THIS socket started are aborted
@enduml

@startuml capability-loading
title Tools, plugins, skills, agents — what loads at BOOT vs what is read EVERY TURN

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #888888
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

package "BOOT — main/container.py (the composition root: the ONLY place things get wired)" as BOOT #FDF6FF {
  folder "plugins/<id>/\nplugin.toml + entry" as PDIR
  folder "agents/<id>/plugins/\n(agent-PRIVATE plugins)" as APDIR
  folder "agents/<id>/\nagent.toml + IDENTITY.md" as ADIR
  rectangle "discover_plugin_contributions\n→ tools + prompt sections\n+ MCP servers + plugin skills" as DISC
  rectangle "discover_agent_plugins\n→ {agent_id: [private tools]}\n(tagged _agent_id)" as ADISC
  rectangle "_gate_and_wrap — EVERY tool's entry treatment\napply_enablement (global on/off)\n→ apply_plugin_enablement (per-tool config)\n→ GuardedTool (timeout · retry · error-norm)\n→ source tag (plugin:<id> / mcp:<srv>)" as GATE
  rectangle "FileAgentRegistry\nagent.toml → frozen AgentSpec\n(allow/deny · skills · model ·\n[plugins.*] overrides · [app])" as REG
  rectangle "NativeEngine\nLiteLLM stream + brain model\n+ failover + compaction + router" as ENG
}

rectangle "AgentService (application)\nholds: shared catalog · private map ·\nregistry · engine · build_prompt" as SVC #F0FFF0

PDIR -down-> DISC
APDIR -down-> ADISC
DISC -down-> GATE
ADISC -down-> GATE
ADIR -down-> REG
GATE -down-> SVC : tools=… / agent_tools={…}
REG -down-> SVC
ENG -down-> SVC

package "EVERY TURN — AgentService.handle_message (nothing cached that shouldn't be)" as TURN #F0FFF0 {
  rectangle "1. resolve the agent\nexplicit agentId | session key | default" as S1
  rectangle "2. set RunContext (contextvar)\nagent_id · workspace (project ws if\nproject chat) · [plugins.*] overrides\n— how a SHARED tool knows who's calling" as S2
  rectangle "3. select tools\nselect_tools(shared, spec)  «allow/deny»\n+ select_private_tools(own)  «deny only»\n→ apply_mode (interactive/cron/heartbeat)" as S3
  rectangle "4. read skills FRESH from disk\nmain/skills (global) + plugin skills\n+ agent's OWN (same name overrides)\n→ eligibility + optional relevance top-K" as S4
  rectangle "5. build the system prompt\nidentity + skills listing + tool guidance\n+ workspace manifest + plugin sections\n+ @mention directive + roster + recall" as S5
  rectangle "6. engine.run(…)\nstream LLM ↔ execute tools until agent_end\nmodel = agent.toml override | brain\n(each TOOL resolves ITS model separately\nvia resolve_tool_model + RunContext)" as S6
}

SVC -down-> S1
S1 -right-> S2
S2 -right-> S3
S3 -down-> S6
S4 -right-> S5
S5 -right-> S6

note bottom of TURN
  HOT-RELOAD: a marketplace install (or the create_tool tool) calls
  register_plugin_live → new shared tools join the LIVE catalog and the
  private map is replaced wholesale — no restart. SKILLS need no reload
  at all: they are read from disk on every turn, so edit → next message.
end note
@enduml
